 ## Background
-The Rational Bézier Deblocking Filter was introduced by F. Marton, José A. Iglesias Guitián, Jose Díaz, and Enrico Gobbetti in the paper "Real-time Deblocked GPU Rendering of Compressed Volumes" (2014) [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It was developed to address the visual quality degradation caused by blocking artifacts in compressed volumetric data during real-time GPU rendering [S1, unofficial]. The method extends deferred filtering architectures to support adaptive multi-resolution data loading and levels of detail [S1, unofficial].
+The Rational Bézier Deblocking Filter was proposed by F. Marton, José A. Iglesias Guitián, Jose Díaz, and Enrico Gobbetti in the paper "Real-time Deblocked GPU Rendering of Compressed Volumes" (2014) [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It extends previous work on deferred filtering for GPU volume rendering [S1, unofficial]. The method addresses the visual quality degradation caused by aggressive compression of massive volumetric datasets, enabling real-time exploration of animated sequences by storing data on the graphics board [S1, unofficial].
 
